@startuml 25-profile-sequence
!include _sequence.iuml
title Profile — written with the questions of the AI, saved, then another profile chosen

actor Reader
participant "Client (React)" as Client
participant "profileRouter\n+ activeProfile" as Router
participant "profileController" as Controller
participant profileService as Profile
participant profileFunnel as Funnel
participant profileAi as AI
participant "ollama\n(gemma4:31b)" as Ollama
participant "embedder\n(bge-m3)" as Embedder
participant profileModel as ProfileModel
participant discoveryService as Discovery
database "PostgreSQL" as DB

== The AI asks, then writes the profile (nothing saved) ==

Reader -> Client : a few words ("Le tennis."), the language read in
loop up to 3 rounds, while the AI asks
    Client -> Router : POST /profile/funnel/questions\n{start, rounds, language}
    note right of Router
        no account needed while accounts can be
        made (signupOpen), else a token;
        40 calls an hour per address
    end note
    Router -> Controller : funnelQuestions(req)
    Controller -> Profile : funnelQuestions({start, rounds, language})
    Profile -> Profile : funnelOf: start 3 to 300 characters,\na language of the list; cleanRounds
    Profile -> Funnel : nextQuestions(funnel)
    Funnel -> Ollama : ollamaJson(questionsPrompt)
    Ollama --> Funnel : {enough, questions}
    Funnel -> Funnel : 2 to 4 questions, 4 to 8 choices each;\na question passed before left out
    Funnel --> Profile : {enough, questions}
    Profile --> Client : {enough, questions, maxRounds}
    Reader -> Client : ticks choices, writes their own words
end
note right of Funnel
    The first round always asks for
    other subjects; the last one at the
    latest asks what the reader refuses
    and, with two subjects or more, which
    ones are followed from afar (weight 0.85)
end note
Client -> Router : POST /profile/funnel/text {start, rounds, language}
Router -> Controller : funnelText(req)
Controller -> Profile : funnelText(asked)
Profile -> Funnel : writeProfile(funnel)
Funnel -> Ollama : ollamaJson(writePrompt)
Ollama --> Funnel : {text}, in the first person
alt under 20 characters
    Profile --> Client : 422, tick or write a little more
end
Profile --> Client : {text}
Reader -> Client : reads the text, changes it if they want

== Saved: the interests read by the AI, their vectors, the discovery started ==

alt the profile shown written again
    Client -> Router : PUT /profile {text, language}
    Router -> ProfileModel : idsOf(user)
    Router -> Controller : save(req)
    Controller -> Profile : save(userId, profileId, {text, language})
else another profile (administrators only, 15 at most)
    Client -> Router : POST /profile/profiles {name, text, language}
    Router -> Controller : create(req)
    Controller -> Profile : create(userId, {name, text, language})
end
note right of Client
    The signup saves the first profile the same
    way, before the account (20-signup-sequence)
end note

Profile -> Profile : prepare: text 20 to 3000 characters,\na language of the list
Profile -> AI : interestsOf({text, language, categories})
AI -> Ollama : ollamaJson(interestsPrompt)
Ollama --> AI : {interests, refused}
AI -> AI : normalizeInterests: 6 at most,\n500 characters each, weight 0.5 to 1,\na category of the list; the refusals cut\nout of the texts, keywords and searches
opt a word of the reader in no interest, or an interest over 500 characters
    AI -> Ollama : ollamaJson(the prompt, its answer,\nwhat to fix)
    Ollama --> AI : the whole answer again
    AI -> AI : the second answer kept when better\non one, not worse on the other
end
AI --> Profile : {interests, refused}
note right of AI
    Each interest: its text (the subject and every
    precision of the reader), weight, keywords,
    Google News searches in up to 4 languages,
    sections, category. "refused" is never an
    interest: its vector would bring those news
end note
alt no interest read
    Profile --> Client : 422
end
Profile -> Embedder : embed(the texts of the interests)
Embedder --> Profile : a dense and a sparse vector each
Profile -> ProfileModel : save(userId, profileId, {text, languages, refused, name}, interests)
ProfileModel -> DB : one transaction: user_profiles written,\nthe interests of the profile replaced\n(not the ones of its projects), their vectors
Profile -> Discovery : start(profileId)
Discovery -> ProfileModel : setDiscovery('running')
Discovery -->> Profile : returns at once
note right of Discovery
    the sources are found in background
    (23-discovery-sequence)
end note
Profile -> Profile : get(userId, profileId)
Profile --> Client : the profile, its interests, sources,\nprojects, every profile of the reader

== The reader chooses another of their profiles ==

Client -> Router : GET /profile/profiles
Router -> Controller : list(req)
Controller -> Profile : list(userId)
Profile -> ProfileModel : ofUser(userId)
Profile --> Client : {profiles: [{id, name}]}
Reader -> Client : chooses one
Client -> Client : setActiveProfile(id), kept in the browser
note right of Client
    every call sends it in the header X-Profile:
    the profile page, the briefing, the sources,
    what the profile follows
end note
Client -> Router : GET /profile (X-Profile: id)
Router -> ProfileModel : idsOf(user)
Router -> Router : activeProfile: req.profileId = the id asked\nif it is one of the user, else their first one
Router -> Controller : get(req)
Controller -> Profile : get(userId, profileId)
par read at once
    Profile -> ProfileModel : owned, interests, projects,\nprojectInterests, removedSources
else
    Profile -> Profile : the sources found (listUserFeeds), the ones\nthe thumbs left out (refusedSources),\nthe Google News searches (searchesOfUser)
else
    Profile -> ProfileModel : profileFeedRelevance
    note right : the news of 14 days of each source\non the interests, kept 15 minutes
end
Profile --> Client : the profile chosen and its data
@enduml
